---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How long does it take to move from Squeegee to Servogo?",
    a: "Most people do it in an evening. Export your clients from Squeegee as CSV. Import into Servogo. Column names are recognised automatically, so there's nothing to remap. Your rounds, addresses, and frequencies land as they were. Email us during the trial if you want a hand.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does Servogo do differently from Squeegee?",
    a: "Drag-drop stop reordering with live arrival-time recalculation, a weather panel on the day view, and payroll tracking per technician. Both tools handle scheduling, invoicing, card payments, and quotes, so the day-to-day basics are covered either way.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will I lose my service history when I switch?",
    a: "Your historical visit records from Squeegee don't transfer across automatically, but your client list, service plans, and frequencies all come across via CSV import. Going forward, Servogo builds a full visit history from every completed job.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a free trial?",
    a: "Yes. 14 days, no card required. You get the full Team plan during the trial. Import your Squeegee data, run the schedule for a week, and decide from there.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will I lose my round history when I switch?",
    a: "Your client list, prices and visit frequencies import from a Squeegee CSV. You keep the round you have built and start fresh records from the day you move.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to remap the columns when I import?",
    a: "No. Servogo reads a standard Squeegee export, so the import recognises the columns without you matching fields one by one.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can my customers pay by card?",
    a: "Yes. Servogo connects to Stripe, so an invoice can be paid online in a couple of taps.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a contract?",
    a: "No long contract. There is a free trial, and you pay monthly after that.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Squeegee Alternative | Servogo: UK Field Service Software"
  description="A Squeegee alternative for UK window cleaners and trades. Import your Squeegee CSV, plan rounds, take Stripe payments and run payroll. Free trial."
  pageType="comparison"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Squeegee alternative', url: '/squeegee-alternative' }]}
>

<section class="page-hero section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Squeegee alternative</span>
      <h1>A Squeegee alternative built for the same trades, with more where it matters</h1>
      <p>
        Servogo is field service software for UK window cleaners, gardeners, and other recurring-service trades.
        It imports your Squeegee client list without any remapping, then adds live route recalculation, a weather panel, and payroll tracking on top.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="https://app.servogo.co.uk/signup" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Start free trial
          <svg class="arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 7h8M8 3l4 4-4 4"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/vs-squeegee" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Full comparison</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-meta" style="justify-content: flex-start;">
        <span><svg class="check" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7.5l3 3 7-7"/></svg> Squeegee CSV import built in</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span>14-day free trial</span>
        <span class="sep"></span>
        <span>No card required</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Switching</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Moving across from Squeegee</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <p>You do not have to rebuild your round from scratch. Export your client list from Squeegee as a CSV and import it straight into Servogo. Names, addresses, prices and visit frequencies come across in one go, so a round you have spent years building is ready the same afternoon.</p>
      <p>Once your clients are in, Servogo works the way a round already works in your head. Set a job to repeat every 4, 6 or 8 weeks and it schedules itself. Open the day and your stops are ordered into a sensible driving route instead of a list you have to plan in your head. Mark a job done and the invoice is ready to send. Payments come in through Stripe, so customers can pay by card without you chasing a bank transfer.</p>
      <p>The difference most people notice is the admin. Less time at the kitchen table on a Sunday working out who owes what, more evenings back. If you run a team, you can see who did which jobs and what they are owed without adding up worksheets by hand.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Why switch</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">What stands out about Servogo.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 11.5a3 3 0 1 0 6 0 3 3 0 1 0-6 0z"/><path d="M12 2C7.5 2 4 5.5 4 10c0 6 8 12 8 12s8-6 8-12c0-4.5-3.5-8-8-8z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Live route recalculation</h3>
        <p>Drag a stop and arrival times update live across the rest of the day. The map redraws as you go, so you always see the real plan.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M6.3 17.7l-1.4 1.4M19.1 4.9l-1.4 1.4"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Weather on the day view</h3>
        <p>Current conditions and the hourly forecast sit right next to your stops, so you can plan the round around the rain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card reveal">
        <div class="feature-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Payroll tracking for your team</h3>
        <p>Set a flat rate or commission per visit for each technician. Servogo calculates earnings from completed jobs, by pay period, ready to export as a CSV when you pay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="deep">
      <div class="deep-copy reveal">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Migration</span>
        <h2>Your Squeegee clients are in Servogo tonight.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Export your Squeegee client list to CSV. Drop it into Servogo's import dialog. Squeegee's column names are recognised automatically. No remapping, no reformatting, no spreadsheet surgery.</p>
        <ul class="deep-list">
          <li>
            <span class="check"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6.5l2.5 2.5L10 3"/></svg></span>
            <span><strong>Clients, addresses, and service plans land intact.</strong> Your rounds, frequencies, and prices come across exactly as they were in Squeegee.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="check"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6.5l2.5 2.5L10 3"/></svg></span>
            <span><strong>Test it during the free trial.</strong> Import your data, run the schedule for a week, see how it fits. No commitment until you're ready.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="check"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6.5l2.5 2.5L10 3"/></svg></span>
            <span><strong>Help available if you need it.</strong> Email us during the trial and we'll walk you through the import. Real people, not automated responses.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a href="https://app.servogo.co.uk/signup" class="btn btn-primary">Start free, import Squeegee data</a>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-shot reveal">
        <div class="browser-bar">
          <div class="browser-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="browser-url">app.servogo.co.uk / schedule</div>
          <div style="width: 50px;"></div>
        </div>
        <img src="/assets/screen-schedule.png" alt="Servogo schedule after Squeegee migration" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Squeegee alternative, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <FAQ items={faqs} />
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 22px); color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0;">
        Related
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <a href="/vs-squeegee" class="btn btn-secondary">Servogo vs Squeegee: full comparison</a>
      <a href="/window-cleaning-software" class="btn btn-secondary">Window cleaning software</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
